// KNOWN LIMITATION — should verify, currently rejected.
//
// The completeness price of guard-aware `merge_chunks`
// (`tests/cases/failing/guarded_merge_chunks.vpr`). When the two merged chunks'
// presence guards differ, each amount is folded into its own gate and the total
// becomes `(b ? 1/2 : 0) + 1/2` — a single opaque `AddR` leaf. Reading `x.f`
// needs `0 < that`, which holds on both branches (`1/1` under `b`, `1/2` under
// `!b`) but not by any const-fold the e-graph can do over an opaque `ite`
// summand, and the perm carries no `ChunkPerm::Select` structure to case-split
// on. Before the guard fix this proved trivially, because the guard was dropped
// and the sum const-folded to `1/1` — which is exactly the unsoundness.
//
// # Why the total is flattened rather than kept as a `Select`
//
// Distributing the sum over the differing guard literal (`perm_add`, which
// already does this) would give `Select(b, 3/2, 1/2)` in the *unsound* shape and
// `Select(b, 1/1, 1/2)` here, and per-leaf proving would discharge this file. But
// `assume_location_axioms` assumes the permission bound **per leaf**, gated only
// by the chunk-level guard — which is empty on the guards-differ path. A `3/2`
// leaf would then fold the bound to `false` ungated and reopen the hole. Making
// the total a `Select` therefore requires teaching the bound axiom to carry each
// arm's branch condition into its gate; until then the sound flattening stands.
//
// Fix direction: gate the per-leaf bound fact by the `Select` conditions
// accumulated on the path to that leaf, then build the total with `perm_add`.
//
// Costs nothing on the corpus: `benchmarks/rust/check.sh` is unchanged at
// 4494 verified / 5 known-failing across the fix.

field f: Int

method guarded_half_still_reads(x: Ref, b: Bool)
{
    if (b) {
        inhale acc(x.f, 1/2)
    }
    inhale acc(x.f, 1/2)
    // Holds `1/2` unconditionally and `1/1` under `b`, so the read frames on
    // every path — but only through a case split on `b`.
    assert x.f == x.f
}
